  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tackling forced and child labour in Ghanaian Cocoa and Goldmining</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project&#x2019;s expected effect(s) on society is that Children and vulnerable people in cocoa and gold-mining communities in Ghana have increased socio-economic resilience and are protected against forced labour and the Worst Forms of Child Labour (WFCL) (Impact).

The expected effects for the target groups of the Project are threefold (Outcomes): 
Outcome 1: The Ghanaian government at a district, regional and national level has implemented efforts to prevent, identify, and address forced labour and WFCL and to protect vulnerable groups.
Outcome 2: Cocoa companies, traders, cooperatives, farmer groups and gold associations have implemented efforts to prevent, identify and address forced labour and the WFCL in their company operations and supply chains, in Ghana, Cd&apos;I, and globally.
Outcome 3: Vulnerable individuals and groups are resilient in the face of recruitment to forced labour and children are protected against the WFCL.

The intended target groups are vulnerable children, youth, women and vulnerable adults in cocoa growing and gold mining communities.</narrative>
  </description>
